/-!
# Cover-parabolic constructions for 13.8.21(2)

The actual T-action selects an invariant native hexad in the Mathieu branch.
Its lifted residual supplies K₁ < K in L(KT,T), and its two-core quotient is
a genuine triple cover of A₆. The actual conjugation action has solvable
kernel, so the model solvable-overgroup comparison lifts to H ∩ M: K₁ is
a C-component of the overlap, or K₁ = K and an actual element of T moves
the two source A₆ parabolic types.

The six-letter geometry supplies ordinary maximality and marked joins
through specified quotient maps. The marked Mathieu and reduced-six modules
now expose the two replacement/parabolic branches with their actual source
coordinates. The final module-recognition contradiction remains downstream.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, p.956 (PDF p.973).
-/
